--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Majik links roughly 900 Rust crates. The great majority are dual MIT OR
Apache-2.0; the components below are the ones carrying obligations or caveats
worth naming. `cargo license` over Cargo.lock produces the exhaustive list.

Apache-2.0 (notice retention required)
  gpui, gpui_platform and the other GPUI crates
    Copyright Zed Industries, Inc. — https://github.com/zed-industries/zed
  gpui-component, gpui-base
    Copyright Longbridge — https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-component

  Apache-2.0 is one-way compatible with GPL-3.0: Apache-licensed code may be
  combined into this GPL-3.0 work. It would not be compatible with GPL-2.0,
  which is why Majik is GPL-3.0-or-later rather than v2.

MPL-2.0 (file-level copyleft; modified files must be published)
  symphonia and its twelve companion crates (audio demux and decode)
  dwrote (Windows text), option-ext
  Majik does not modify these crates, so no source publication is owed.

MIT (bundled assets, not linked code)
  HugeIcons — the icons in crates/majik-app/assets/icons are generated from the free
  @hugeicons/core-free-icons package. https://hugeicons.com

Trademarks (bundled assets, not licensed under the GPL)
  crates/majik-app/assets/logos holds the wordmarks and logos of the providers and
  model vendors Majik can call — fal, Replicate, OpenRouter, OpenAI, Google, Meta,
  ByteDance, Alibaba, Runway, ElevenLabs, Kling, MiniMax, Pixverse, Recraft, LTX,
  Veed, Sourceful, Flux, Grok among them. They are the trademarks of their
  respective owners and are reproduced nominatively, to identify which provider or
  model a generation came from. No affiliation with or endorsement by those owners
  is claimed. Majik's GPL-3.0 grant covers Majik's own code and assets; it does not
  grant any right in these marks, and it is not a licence to use them. Anyone
  redistributing a modified Majik under a different name should replace them.

BSD-2-Clause
  openh264, openh264-sys2 — Copyright Cisco Systems, Inc.

  H.264 patents: Majik builds openh264 from source (`features = ["source"]`).
  Cisco's royalty-free arrangement with the AVC patent pool covers Cisco's own
  precompiled binaries, not third-party builds, so AVC patent licensing for
  distributed Majik binaries is not covered by that arrangement.

Other licences present in the dependency tree: MIT, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Zlib,
Unicode-3.0, BSL-1.0, CC0-1.0 and Unlicense. No GPL- or AGPL-licensed
dependency is linked; nothing in the tree imposes an obligation beyond those
named above.
